Forces $\mathbf{F}_1$, $\mathbf{F}_2$ and $\mathbf{F}_3$ are such that

- $\mathbf{F}_1 = (-\mathbf{i} + 3\mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k})\ \mathrm{N}$ and acts through the point with position vector $(3\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j} - 3\mathbf{k})\ \mathrm{m}$;
- $\mathbf{F}_2 = (2\mathbf{i} + 4\mathbf{j} - 4\mathbf{k})\ \mathrm{N}$ and acts through the point with position vector $(3\mathbf{i} + 2\mathbf{j} - 4\mathbf{k})\ \mathrm{m}$;
- $\mathbf{F}_3$ has magnitude $7\ \mathrm{N}$ and acts along the line $\mathbf{r} = 8\mathbf{i} + 3\mathbf{j} + \mu(6\mathbf{i} + 3\mathbf{j} + 2\mathbf{k})$.
